VERDICT (structural; no QED):
  1. The double-commutator identity is TRUE and its direction is UP: it pins the FIRST
     MOMENT of nu_w, hence gives upper bounds (w1 <= Ebar/s1) and no floor.
  2. The only exact lower bound is the residue-level-gap lemma w1 >= (s2-Ebar)/(s2-s1):
     sharp, and after [A] its ONLY non-computable input is s2 = the channel isolation.
  3. It FIRES on the double well (w1~0.97, bound~0.9x) => not a YM mechanism; and in YM the
     moment is UV-dominated (Ebar ~ a^-2 bare / ~1/t flowed) so it is vacuous until the
     fixed-scale window of U4 S3.1 is entered -- inside which it IS isolation.
  4. w1 is measurable in principle (a ratio of correlator quantities) but the existing
     L=4..8 data at N=2000 are contact-dominated: no L-trend of w1 is extractable.
